cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  multiomics_OT: optimal-transport correspondence, ambiguity detection and
  upgrades for single-cell multi-omics integration and label transfer
message: If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mehran
    family-names: Piran
    email: m.piran@unsw.edu.au
    affiliation: School of Biotechnology and Biomolecular Sciences, UNSW Sydney
  - given-names: Fatemeh
    family-names: Vafaee
    email: f.vafaee@unsw.edu.au
    affiliation: School of Biotechnology and Biomolecular Sciences, UNSW Sydney
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7521-2417
repository-code: https://github.com/VafaeeLab/multiomics_OT
abstract: >-
  Single-cell multi-omics methods align cells across modalities, integrate them
  into one embedding and transfer labels between them. All three steps depend on
  a match between cells in two modalities, and that match is usually hidden
  inside each tool, so every cell looks equally certain. This software makes the
  match explicit as a soft coupling matrix built with optimal transport, scores
  how uncertain each cell's match is, and uses that score to upgrade existing
  integration and label-transfer tools without retraining them.
keywords:
  - single-cell multi-omics
  - optimal transport
  - data integration
  - label transfer
  - ambiguity detection
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: Optimal transport reveals unresolved cells in single-cell multi-omics
